---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Weight Tracker & Weight Loss Progress | Nawtch"
  description="Log your daily weight and see trends over time with Nawtch's free, private weight tracker. Switch lb and kg — your data never leaves your device."
  canonicalPath="/weight/"
>
  <header>
    <div class="header-left">
      <h1>Weight Tracker</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Track your body weight, monitor weight loss progress, and view trends over time with a private weight tracker.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="date-badge">
      <div class="date-day" id="wt-hdr-date">—</div>
      <div class="date-reset">Once per day</div>
    </div>
  </header>
  <div id="tab-weight"></div>
  <div class="info-banners">
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--accent2);box-shadow:0 0 6px var(--accent2);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-warn">Log once per day, update anytime</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Logging today's weight switches the button to <strong>Update</strong> instead of <strong>Save</strong>, so entering a new number always edits today's single entry rather than creating a duplicate. You can
        update it as many times as you want during the day — only the latest value is kept.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--muted);box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--muted);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-info">Switch between lb and kg anytime</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Your unit choice (<strong>lb</strong> or <strong>kg</strong>) is shared with the Settings page, and
        every entry is stored normalized in kilograms internally. Switching units only changes how numbers are
        displayed — it never changes the underlying data or any entry you've already logged.
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="info-banner">
      <div class="info-banner-header" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
        <div class="info-dot" style="background:var(--carbs);box-shadow: 0 0 6px var(--carbs);"></div>
        <span class="info-banner-label info-label-warn-2">Log at the same time of day for a trend that means something</span>
        <span class="info-banner-chevron">▼</span>
      </div>
      <div class="info-banner-body">
        Body weight can swing a few pounds or kilograms in a single day from food, water, and hydration alone —
        not just fat loss or gain. Logging at roughly the same time each day (first thing in the morning is
        typical) makes the <strong>Weight Over Time</strong> chart's trend far more meaningful than any single
        day's number.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="field-hint" style="display:block;margin-top:14px;">
    Wondering what your numbers mean? Check your <a href="/calculators/bmi/">BMI</a>, <a href="/calculators/ideal-weight/">ideal weight range</a>, or <a href="/calculators/body-fat/">body fat %</a>.
  </p>

  <!-- ECharts CDN -->
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/echarts@5.5.0/dist/echarts.min.js" defer></script>
  <script src="../../islands/vanilla/weight/weight.js"></script>
</BaseLayout>
